  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run accumulated substantial HP loss after the early floors and reached the Slime Boss with only 49/87 HP. The final combat then became a survival problem: at very low HP, several turns spent on defensive or setup actions did not sufficiently reduce the remaining threats. The deck also adopted a narrow Perfected Strike plan without much supporting Strike density.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "CARD_REWARD",
        "title": "Avoid narrow Perfected Strike without enough Strike support",
        "situation": "When Perfected Strike is offered early and the current deck does not already contain several Strike cards or other cards with Strike in their names.",
        "lesson": "Treat Perfected Strike as a scaling commitment rather than a generic attack. Prefer skipping or taking a broader payoff unless the deck is already clearly supporting it; adding more basic attacks later is not guaranteed.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "At Act 1 Floor 10, Perfected Strike was chosen over Reaper, Twin Strike, or skipping.",
          "The final 16-card deck contained four Strikes, four Defends, and only one Perfected Strike; it had no other Strike-named cards."
        ],
        "reasoning": "The final build shows that Perfected Strike had only a limited number of qualifying cards to scale from, so the reward choice committed to a synergy that was not substantially developed by the end of the act.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "At critical HP, stop spending turns on low-impact setup",
        "situation": "When HP is already in lethal range and enemies have attack intents, especially when the hand contains meaningful attacks alongside weak setup or defense.",
        "lesson": "Reassess every energy expenditure for immediate survival or lethal progress. Do not automatically chain small blocks and setup cards; use the strongest available damage line when it can remove or substantially weaken an attacker, while recognizing that exact damage counterfactuals require the full combat state.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "On Turn 8 at 13/87 HP, with Acid Slime attacking and Thunderclap, Bash, Pommel Strike, and Strike available, the actions were Defend+, Pommel Strike, and Armaments; the next logged state was 6/87 HP.",
          "On Turn 10 at 6/87 HP, both enemies had ATTACK_DEBUFF intents; Defend was played before Uppercut, leaving no recorded opportunity to resolve the available Perfected Strike+ that turn."
        ],
        "reasoning": "These states show the run was already at an emergency HP threshold, yet energy was partly spent on defense or upgrading rather than maximizing immediate threat reduction. The log does not prove a specific alternative would have won, so this is a sequencing hypothesis rather than a guaranteed counterfactual.",
        "confidence": "medium"
      },
      {
        "category": "REST",
        "title": "Preserve enough HP before the boss to make combat decisions flexible",
        "situation": "After repeated hallway damage, when entering the boss with substantial missing HP and no healing potion.",
        "lesson": "Treat HP as a resource needed for multiple future turns, not merely for surviving the next room. When the boss is close and the deck lacks reliable sustain, favor healing or safer fights over choices that leave the run dependent on perfect early combat draws.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "HP fell from 80/80 on Floor 1 to 49/80 after the Floor 4 combat, then to 30/87 by Floor 12 and 23/87 by Floor 14.",
          "The boss combat began at 49/87 HP, and the detailed log reached 13/87 on Turn 8, 6/87 on Turn 9, and 0 HP shortly afterward."
        ],
        "reasoning": "The repeated HP decline left little tolerance for the Slime Boss's multi-enemy phase. Although the Floor 15 rest improved the starting total, the run still entered the boss with only a little over half health and no potions, making later combat sequencing much less forgiving.",
        "confidence": "high"
      }
